  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Slosh. Logic: rules.objective and rules.gameplay; place engine then play to the left; slosh when previous player could not play on own train.',
    Player: 'Slosh is a four-handed British domino game from the Trains family. Double-six set; each player has a train from the center engine. Add a tile to your own train if you can; if you cannot, the next player may slosh (play on your train) then play on their own. Lowest pip count when the round ends (domino or blocked) wins; domino scores zero.',
    objective: 'Win rounds by dominoing (emptying your hand) or having the lowest pip count when the game is blocked. The lowest scorer is paid the difference by each other player.',
    gameplay: 'The engine is placed in the center. Each player has a train extending from the engine toward them (traditionally the four trains extend diagonally from the four corners of the engine). On your turn, add a tile to your own train if you can, matching the open end. If you cannot play, the next player may slosh (play a tile on your train) before adding a tile to their own train. If the previous player could play on their train, you may only play on your own train. The round ends when someone dominoes or the game is blocked; hands are scored by pips left (domino scores zero).',
    keyRules: [
      'Engine for each round: double-four, then double-five, double-six, double-one, double-two, double-three.',
      'Player with engine places it first; play to the left.',
      'Add to own train if possible; if not, next player may slosh then play on own train.',
      'Lowest pip count wins the round; domino scores zero; lowest is paid the difference by others.',
